ulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d4a59fe-0871-5826-aa72-1fb9c0a2dad6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105431" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 6,\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 3}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}<9,\\,1<{y}^{2}<16}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2},\\,-2\\le x\\le 2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,\\sqrt{3}).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e3f425a-0a1f-515b-8c03-990715e116f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470835} {:answer/id #uuid "46c61006-9d69-5224-84b5-adb4594d575a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c61006-9d69-5224-84b5-adb4594d575a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470836} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24fe181-c890-5457-b487-5bd9845a29a6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "455ea2d6-36ea-506e-8abc-4fb2725d1508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470837} {:answer/id #uuid "b1bbc0e3-f77f-5075-b7c1-c24869a40657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "455ea2d6-36ea-506e-8abc-4fb2725d1508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470837} :answer-field/id #uuid "523aebc4-d33b-5507-8bcd-9a008fe77b20" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a53fe6cb-2b4e-5db2-a7b8-cf233dd5a07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470839} {:answer/id #uuid "0c743f3a-ed2f-55ac-b5d2-1af41de6baef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a53fe6cb-2b4e-5db2-a7b8-cf233dd5a07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470839} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ebafac-d103-5f82-9a2a-34326808b7f4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f4b0cdf-9fe1-57d6-a009-4edf0331d401" :question/math-academy-id "q-105444" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,6\\le x<9,\\,0<y<2}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}<3}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(6,1).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(8,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is also *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f462a13-e52b-5f50-bd9b-5e3e04a75ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465417} {:answer/id #uuid "7d035b1f-7fbf-59ff-b61e-ebb312eee7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d035b1f-7fbf-59ff-b61e-ebb312eee7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465418} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4834f1a-3776-5597-bca0-28aea74896d7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4acc30dd-b0dd-5587-9188-4cc8367a69bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465419} {:answer/id #uuid "28f06c85-e623-54b7-9f55-9afd7009566f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28f06c85-e623-54b7-9f55-9afd7009566f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465420} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac548899-74b4-5b42-b1ca-0d1482e4229f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb0fe9bc-f78c-5c55-bbf7-fd65e2ea1195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465421} {:answer/id #uuid "c615d31d-cf76-5762-8eca-1a561a4f0997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb0fe9bc-f78c-5c55-bbf7-fd65e2ea1195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465421} :answer-field/id #uuid "28fa83d6-4600-547a-a25c-706ebb06a453" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fb05970-59dc-5904-9b90-0c1d735b4269" :question/math-academy-id "q-161638" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le 3}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1<x<1,\\,0<y<2-{x}^{2}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16604ddb-69ca-5ace-9dbf-0383a82ea98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471113} {:answer/id #uuid "ed093c42-08ca-5342-9c3d-5d707ac0618a" :answer/type {:db/id #e